/*
	RMSTEST 7 — is avoid_actor_area checked per member under TIGHT grouping?

	This is the one row in docs/preview-design.md Sec.6.6's grouping-scope table
	that the guide never rules on directly. Every other row cites a per-attribute
	entry; the actor-area row rests entirely on the tight/loose illustrative
	lists at guide:2122 / guide:2143, so it has no source at all.

	Test 1 and Test 6 established: tight = one anchor checked, then unchecked
	fill; loose = every member checked. If that generalises, avoid_actor_area
	under tight grouping should be checked ONLY on the anchor.

	GEOMETRY — everything here is deterministic, no random land placement.
	  The clearing is a 15x15 grass square (base_size 7) at land_position 50 50,
	  which on a 120-wide map is tile (60,60), so it spans 53..67 on both axes.
	  create_actor_area 60 60 1234 5 is a SQUARE radius (guide:1994 — and those
	  coordinates are in TILES, not percent), so it covers 55..65, an 11x11
	  block centred in the clearing.
	  Valid tiles for the gold are therefore the clearing MINUS the actor area:
	  a 2-tile-wide border ring, 225 - 121 = 104 tiles. Plenty for 25 objects.

	Player lands are pushed out to circle_radius 45 and made DESERT so they
	cannot be confused with the central grass clearing.

	READ IT LIKE THIS
	  Gold sits in the central 11x11 block (or spills into it from the ring)
	      -> anchor-only. avoid_actor_area follows Test 1's rule, and Sec.6.6's
	         actor-area row should be folded into the general tight rule.
	  Gold sits ONLY in the 2-tile border ring, forming a band or corner shape
	  and leaving a clean square hole in the middle
	      -> checked per MEMBER even under tight grouping. This is the case you
	         suspected, and it means the tight rule is not uniform: some
	         attributes are enforced during the fill and some are not.
	  No gold at all
	      -> re-roll; if it persists, the actor area is being read differently
	         than assumed (check whether the radius is being treated as
	         Euclidean, which would change the valid set).

	The single STONE pile is a CONTROL on the same land with no avoidance. It
	must appear. If it is missing, the map failed for an unrelated reason.

	Both create_objects carry set_gaia_object_only because Test 3 CONFIRMED that
	a frame-referenced non-ownable object without it places nothing — and
	place_on_specific_land_id is a reference frame.

	RUN ON: Tiny, 2 players. There is only one clearing that matters, at the
	exact centre of the map, so one sample per seed.
*/

<PLAYER_SETUP>
random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
base_terrain FOREST

create_player_lands
{
	terrain_type DESERT
	base_size 3
	number_of_tiles 1
	circle_radius 45 0
}

create_land
{
	terrain_type GRASS
	land_position 50 50
	base_size 7
	number_of_tiles 1
	land_id 5
	zone 7
}

<OBJECTS_GENERATION>

create_actor_area 60 60 1234 5

/* THE TEST: tight group that must avoid the central 11x11 block. */
create_object GOLD
{
	number_of_objects 25
	set_tight_grouping
	set_gaia_object_only
	place_on_specific_land_id 5
	avoid_actor_area 1234
}

/* CONTROL: same land, no avoidance. Must appear. */
create_object STONE
{
	number_of_objects 1
	set_gaia_object_only
	place_on_specific_land_id 5
}
